	"nodes":[
		{"id":"fb2aee3576edc84a","type":"text","text":"## Financial Services Industry\n\n**Links** **savers** who have money with **spenders** who need money.\n\nOffers **services** to savers and spenders and **channels** funds between them.\n\n* **Savers**\n\t* Individuals\n\t* Households\n\t* Companies\n\t* Governments\n* **Spenders**\n\t* Individuals borrowing for personal expense (housing, education)\n\t* companies borrowing for capital investments (machinery, facilities)\n\t* Governments funding budget deficits\n\n\n\n","x":-300,"y":-260,"width":620,"height":480},
		{"id":"eab67cb2e371a320","type":"file","file":"Attachments/Pasted image 20261116151715.png","x":-840,"y":-20,"width":400,"height":217},
		{"id":"cd6814d42481a2d9","type":"text","text":"## Classification of Assets and Capital\n\n* **Real Assets**: Physical/tangible assets such as land, buildings, machinery, cattle and gold.\n\t* **Physical capital** is the means of production (buildings, equipment)\n* **Financial Assets**: Claims on real assets or their earnings (e.g. shares of stock representing ownership or bonds representing debt).\n\n**Financial assets** that can be **traded** are called **securities**. These are traded in **financial markets**.\n\n\n\n","x":-1080,"y":-520,"width":560,"height":400},
		{"id":"1ccca12df6c41ec1","type":"text","text":"## Direct vs Indirect Finance\n\n**Direct Finance**: when providers and users of capital interact, provider has a direct claim on the user e.g. right to earnings.\n\n**Indirect Finance**: use of financial intermediaries between to channel funds between providers and users, so no direct claim.","x":-600,"y":400,"width":680,"height":320}
	],
